priority: HIGH — part of the AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER cluster (operator goal 2026-06-27).
scope: AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER (cluster 3/3). `charon work` closes the loop only PARTIALLY, and its
  quality gate is weaker than it should be. VERIFIED ON origin/master 2026-06-27:
    (a) PR is never opened. `run_work` (cli.py:822) drives each DONE unit through
        `land.land_unit(ledger, list(bu.owns))` (cli.py ~915) — which is READ-ONLY: it commits on a
        DETACHED HEAD (no branch), runs the acceptance gate, and computes a propose/hold verdict,
        but NEVER pushes and NEVER opens a PR. `land.open_pr` (land.py:411) exists but is invoked
        ONLY from the separate `charon land --open-pr` command (cli.py:120-126), never from `work`.
        So an autonomous `work` run produces local commits + a verdict and then STOPS — nothing
        lands as a reviewable PR.
    (b) The real reviewer exists but is NOT wired into the work path. CORRECTION TO EARLIER
        EVIDENCE: `adapters/review.py` is NO LONGER a stub — it now ships `GatewayReviewer`, a
        REAL cross-model consensus reviewer that calls the loopback Charon gateway
        (adapters/review.py:1,69). The deterministic `MockReviewer` moved to
        `adapters/review_mock.py`. BUT: only the `charon run` CLI wires a reviewer, and it wires
        the MOCK (cli.py:41-42,55 → `MockReviewer(ReviewMode(args.review))`). The `work` path
        (`run_work` → `CoordinatorRunner`) passes NO reviewer at all → default L1, NO review gate.
        So `GatewayReviewer` is built but dead-on-arrival for autonomous ticket work, and the only
        quality bar a `work` run applies is the acceptance checks.
  FIX: (a) make `charon work`, BEHIND A FLAG, create a branch + push + call `open_pr` for each
  proposed unit — NEVER auto-merge (preserve propose-default; the human/other-agent merges); and
  (b) wire the existing `GatewayReviewer` (NOT the mock) into the work path so each unit gets a
  real cross-model adversarial review gate, not just acceptance checks.
  MAY SPLIT into two tickets if cleaner: WORK-LAND-PR (a: branch+push+open_pr behind a flag,
  owns cli.py + land.py) and a separate WORK-REAL-REVIEW (b: wire GatewayReviewer into the work
  path, owns review.py + the engine wiring). Decide at activation.
  CONSTRAINTS: NEVER auto-merge — propose-default is non-negotiable (ADR-0010 D5); pushing/PR-open
  stays behind an explicit flag (fail-closed when off); agent/provider-agnostic; product-clean (no
  SLOP/fleet/rig leak); stdlib-only privileged core; the real reviewer routes via the loopback
  gateway, so it composes with WORK-GATEWAY-WIRE.
note: PARKED. Part of the AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER cluster (operator goal 2026-06-27: run real
  tickets via a non-Claude agent through `charon work`). Closing all three (WORK-GATEWAY-WIRE +
  WORK-AGENT-BEARINGS + WORK-LAND-PR), plus WORK-OBSERVABILITY for watching it, makes it
  trustworthy end-to-end. This ticket is what turns a finished unit into a real, reviewed,
  proposable PR — without it the run never produces anything a human can land. Activate when the
  autonomous-runner goal is prioritized.

